OL,3,GNEWSALancashire's 'strong R' due to
OL,4,Ahidden tongue movement, study finds
OL,5,
OL,6,FScientists have observed "hidden"
OL,7,Ftongue movements in one of the last
OL,8,Fplaces in England still using a
OL,9,Fdistinctive pronunciation of the letter
OL,10,FR and they also witnessed a decline in
OL,11,Fthe historical sound.
OL,13,FBy using ultrasound technology,
OL,14,FLancaster University researchers have
OL,15,Fbeen able to watch how the tongue moves
OL,16,Fduring speech.
OL,18,FThe rhoticity study focused on people
OL,19,Fin Blackburn, as its older residents
OL,20,Fstill pronounce a "strong R" sound
OL,21,Fafter vowels in words like star and
OL,22,Fheart.
OL,23,APub: 16-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,404,400,260,160,0,100
